🎯 Interview Questions
Q1. Why separate CRUD logic from routers?
It keeps the code modular. Routers handle HTTP requests, while CRUD functions handle database
operations. This separation makes the application easier to maintain and test.

Q2. Why call db.commit()?

commit() permanently saves the transaction to the database. Without it, changes remain uncommitted and
are lost when the session ends.

Q3. Why call db.refresh()?

After inserting a row, the database generates values such as the primary key and timestamp. refresh()
updates the Python object with those generated values.

